{
  "_comment": [
    "IO element definitions for Teltonika FMB-series devices.",
    "",
    "THIS FILE IS INTENTIONALLY INCOMPLETE. It contains only the AVL ids I",
    "was confident enough to write down. The FMB920 publishes a few hundred.",
    "Before you rely on this in production, open the Teltonika wiki page for",
    "your exact model, find the 'AVL ID' table, and transcribe it.",
    "",
    "Unlisted ids still decode fine. They come out with name null and the",
    "raw integer as the value, so nothing is lost, it is just unlabelled.",
    "",
    "Each entry carries a 'confidence' field:",
    "  verified = byte width confirmed against a real Codec 8 packet",
    "  high     = widely documented",
    "  med      = plausible, verify against the wiki before trusting",
    "",
    "Schema per entry:",
    "  name        display name",
    "  unit        optional, appended to the decoded value",
    "  multiplier  optional, raw is multiplied by this to get value",
    "  signed      optional, treat the raw bytes as two's complement",
    "  enum        optional, maps raw value to a state string",
    "  confidence  documentation only, the parser ignores it"
  ],

  "io_elements": {
